PicoEFI C template
==================

This is a simple C "hello world" program template using PicoEFI.
For information about PicoEFI, see:
https://github.com/PicoEFI/PicoEFI

Works with clang and GCC, no need for any specialised toolchain or set up.
Just type "make run" to build and run the hello world program in QEMU.

Building also requires "git", used to fetch the dependencies (see get-deps),
and "curl", used to download the EDK2 OVMF firmware images for "make run".

Assembly files with the *.S extension are built using the same toolchain as
the C sources. Only *.asm files, which are built for ia32 and x86_64 alone and
of which the template ships none, require "nasm".

The "TOOLCHAIN" and "TOOLCHAIN_PREFIX" make variables can be used to set
the toolchain. "TOOLCHAIN" can be set to "llvm" to use Clang/LLVM.
For example:
    make TOOLCHAIN=llvm
or:
    make TOOLCHAIN_PREFIX=x86_64-elf-
